# The variant that asks what the per-directory documents are worth on
# a real change: every nested AGENTS.md and its CLAUDE.md pointer,
# gone. The root document stays — the pattern's `**` prefix matches at
# depth one and deeper, so the thing being ablated is the nested layer
# and not the harness.
#
# It leaves the root map pointing at documents that are no longer
# there, and that is not a flaw in the measurement: a project whose
# nested docs were never written has no rows either, and a project
# that lost them has exactly this. Read the A/B report's flags — a
# case that stops discriminating under the variant says so.
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
